{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And an ox.</b> And not a beast (חיה)." "<b>Or a lamb.</b> And not fowl." "<b>It and its son.</b> One whose son is bound after it — this excludes a male whose son is not bound after it. Rashi explained here: it does not apply to males, and it is permitted to slaughter the father and the son. The Gaon said: granted there is no liability for lashes, yet there is still a prohibition, as is stated in the chapter אותו ואת בנו."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:26.935033343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}